# The test a_thousand_switches_between_two_integer_contexts of context_switch (#85): a thousand switches between two
# contexts that run integer code only, with the save QEMU's -cpu max offers first, XSAVEOPT, on a debug server kernel
# (./build.sh --server), the test alone selected. x2APIC is left out because QEMU 10.2 stops on "Bad icount read" when
# the kernel runs x2APIC under -icount. Checked by tools/instructions.sh --budget tools/budgets/context-switch.debug.budget
# kernel/lpl.kernel; a change of cpu_context_switch records the new counts. On QEMU's own processor, which has no XSAVE,
# the same window takes FXSAVE: tools/instructions.sh --inside <this window's function> --times 1 --append <its line>
# counts 58,195 instructions and 106,077 accesses there.
inside=kernel_test_body_a_thousand_switches_between_two_integer_contexts
times=1
cpu=max,-x2apic
append=lpl.test=context_switch.a_thousand_switches_between_two_integer_contexts
instructions=58852
accesses=143307
tolerance=1
